# Recurring findings in this repo that are deliberate. One Python regex per line, matched
# against "PATH:MATCH" by the repo-sensitive-scan skill's scanner. Keep this list short and
# specific: a broad pattern here is how a real identifier gets published. Backlog A24 is the
# entry; plans/PEAT_MIGRATION.md §3 says what was redacted and what each placeholder means.

# Test fixtures. These are invented credentials, asserted on by name, and the suite needs
# values shaped like the real thing to prove that rejection and masking work.
^tests/test_auth\.py:(sk-a|pass|----)
^tests/test_settings\.py:sk-a
^tests/test_graph\.py:sk-a

# Placeholder site paths. The campaign netid and the allocation id below are fictitious and
# shaped only so they validate (NETID_RE wants 2-16 alphanumerics); see the Placeholders key
# in plans/AMAREL_ENDPOINT.md. They stay concrete rather than becoming <angle> tokens
# because test fixtures assert on rendered paths.
^.*:/projects/f_proj00_1
^.*:/scratch/abc123
^tests/.*:/projects/(x|with|test)\b
^tests/.*:/projects/\.\.\.

# The cluster's own shared trees: public module and software paths, not anyone's directory.
^.*:/projects/community/modulefiles

# An SSH URL, not an address.
^plans/LINODE_DEPLOY\.md:git@github\.com

# `orbit` is the unprivileged service account the broker and the agent run as, named after
# the software and created by the deployment in plans/LINODE_DEPLOY.md. It names no person,
# and the paths are the documented layout of that host.
^plans/.*:/home/orbit
# Same path quoted in a commit message, where there is no file path to anchor on.
^\(commit message [0-9a-f]+\):/home/orbit

# A literal ellipsis standing in for the rest of a path, in prose.
^plans/.*:/projects/\.\.\.$
